      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's not just the writing though. it's everything. i've been thinking lately about this concept for a poem... about how life is just this long, exhausting performance of staying alive, and how the only way to actually be \"real\" or \"pure\" is to break the cycle. like, there's a certain kind of tragic beauty in the idea that the most honest thing a person can do is finally choose to end the performance. i want to explore that, but i'm struggling to make it sound... i don't know, profound instead of just sad.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
